<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15520" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ēlŏcūtĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop., <i>a speaking out</i>, <i>utterance</i>,
				<i>expression</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pluralis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					22, 5, 12</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, in rhet. lang., <i>oratorical delivery</i>, <i>elocution;</i> the
			Gr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φράσις</span> (cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">locutio, dictio, stilus, etc.),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Inv. 1, 7, 9</span></i>
			; Quint. prooem. § 22; 8 prooem. § 13; 8, 1,
			1 et saep.</div>
